<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37774" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-mŏrĭor</span></b> , tuus,
		3, v. dep., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to die early</i> or <i>prematurely</i>, <i>to die</i> (mostly <b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aut ego praemoriar, primoque exstinguar in
					aevo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					8, 121</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">parte corporis velut praemortua,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet.
					Gram. 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to decay</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praemoritur visus, auditus,</span>”
				<i>decays</i>, <i>fails</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 50, 51, § 168</span></i>
			.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-mortŭus</span></b> , a, um, P.
				a., <i>dead.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jacuere, velut praemortua, membra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 7, 65</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pudor praemortuus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					3, 72, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vires,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. Decl. 12, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
